-- Hand-written interview answer repair: performance, business, personal, press and recording.
WITH tailored(question_text,a,b,c,d) AS (VALUES
('Do stage effects improve a show or distract from the music?', 'Great effects enhance the emotion of the songs.', 'We use visuals sparingly when they suit the set.', 'A powerful lighting cue can turn a chorus into a moment.', 'If the smoke hides the drummer, we''ve gone too far.'),
('Do you change performances for different cities?', 'Yes, every crowd brings out something different in us.', 'We sometimes adjust the setlist for local fans.', 'A city with wild energy deserves a wilder encore.', 'Mostly we adapt when the venue has no backstage stairs.'),
('Have you ever walked off stage unhappy despite a cheering crowd?', 'Yes, because I knew I could have played better.', 'A happy audience matters, but we also assess our own performance.', 'A roaring crowd doesn''t erase a disastrous mistake.', 'I smiled, bowed and then argued with my guitar.'),
('How do you choose which songs get dropped from a setlist?', 'We balance audience favourites with new material.', 'Songs that don''t flow with the set sometimes need a rest.', 'If a track kills momentum, it loses its slot.', 'Usually whichever song needs the most guitar changes.'),
('How important is crowd interaction to you?', 'It''s the moment a performance becomes a shared experience.', 'I like natural conversation rather than rehearsed speeches.', 'Without the crowd, even a perfect show can feel flat.', 'If they sing louder than us, they''re running the gig.'),
('How much of your set is carefully planned versus spontaneous?', 'We build a structure but leave room for surprises.', 'The transitions are planned; the energy changes nightly.', 'Our best moments often happen off the setlist.', 'The encore depends on whether we remember the chords.'),
('What makes a genuinely great live show?', 'Music, connection and a room full of people feeling something.', 'Tight playing matters, but so does taking risks.', 'I''d rather see a flawed show with fire than sterile perfection.', 'A crowd that refuses to leave when the lights come on.'),
('What''s the biggest live mistake you''ve made?', 'I''ve missed a cue and had to recover in front of everyone.', 'Once I started the wrong song and we laughed it off.', 'We turned a complete breakdown into an extended jam.', 'I introduced a song by the wrong title.'),
('Would you ever play a famous song you personally hate because fans demand it?', 'If it means something to fans, I''d reconsider it.', 'We could rearrange it so it feels fresh again.', 'I''d rather earn their respect with songs we believe in.', 'I''d play it once, then retire it on stage.'),
('Would you rather sound perfect or be unpredictable live?', 'Give me honest energy with a few rough edges.', 'I want reliability with space for improvisation.', 'Unpredictability is what makes live music dangerous.', 'Perfect is overrated; just keep the amps on.'),
('Do musicians talk honestly enough about money?', 'Not nearly enough; transparency helps young artists.', 'We should discuss costs as openly as ticket prices.', 'Silence about money protects bad industry deals.', 'I''ll show you the tour receipts if you want.'),
('Do streaming platforms pay artists fairly?', 'The rates need work, especially for emerging musicians.', 'Streaming helps discovery, but the income is inconsistent.', 'Exposure doesn''t cover studio rent or van repairs.', 'Our bass strings probably earned more than the stream did.'),
('Do you think ticket prices are getting too high?', 'Fans shouldn''t have to choose between gigs and groceries.', 'Rising production costs matter, but affordability still counts.', 'Premium pricing can shut out the people who built a fanbase.', 'If a seat costs a fortune, the band should serve dinner.'),
('Has money ever caused tension inside the band?', 'We''ve learned to discuss expenses before they become arguments.', 'We use clear splits and keep the finances transparent.', 'Nothing tests friendship like an unexpected bill.', 'Only when someone charges the band for their snacks.'),
('How important is merchandise income to a modern band?', 'Merch sales make a real difference to touring survival.', 'It''s useful income, but quality matters more than volume.', 'A great shirt can fund the next gig.', 'Please buy a shirt; our van needs new tyres.'),
('How involved are you in the business side of the band?', 'I pay attention because decisions affect everyone.', 'We share responsibility with people we trust.', 'Artists who ignore contracts can lose control of their songs.', 'I read every invoice, usually with growing horror.'),
('Should successful artists charge fans for premium experiences?', 'It''s fine when ordinary fans still get a great show.', 'Paid extras should be optional and genuinely worthwhile.', 'Loyalty shouldn''t be priced out of reach.', 'I''ll charge extra only for my terrible jokes.'),
('Would you ever release music purely because it was commercially safe?', 'I''d rather believe in the song before releasing it.', 'We consider the audience without writing to a formula.', 'A safe single can cost you your identity.', 'Only if the label agrees to call it our joke track.'),
('Would you rather own your masters or take a massive advance?', 'Owning our music gives us control over the future.', 'It depends on the terms and what we''d be giving up.', 'Give me the masters; long-term freedom beats quick cash.', 'How massive is the advance, exactly?'),
('Would you take a huge sponsorship deal from a brand you don''t love?', 'No; our name should stand for something.', 'We''d consider whether the partnership fits our values.', 'Fans would spot a cynical cash grab immediately.', 'Depends whether the sponsor can fix the tour bus.'),
('Do you find it easy to trust new people around the band?', 'Trust takes time and consistent behaviour.', 'We check references and set boundaries early.', 'I''ve learned not every friendly face wants the best for us.', 'If they promise instant fame, I check the exits.'),
('Do you think musicians need an ego to succeed?', 'Confidence helps, but respect matters more.', 'You need self-belief without ignoring other people.', 'A little arrogance can push you to take risks.', 'Mine barely fits in the dressing room.'),
('Have your priorities changed since becoming a working musician?', 'I care more about staying healthy and making honest music.', 'Now I balance creative ambition with practical responsibilities.', 'Success means less if the band falls apart chasing it.', 'I value sleep more than free backstage drinks.'),
('How do you deal with jealousy?', 'I focus on the work instead of comparing careers.', 'I acknowledge the feeling and learn from it.', 'Jealousy can be fuel if it doesn''t become bitterness.', 'I stop scrolling through other bands'' tour announcements.'),
('How do you protect your private life?', 'I share what I''m comfortable with and keep the rest offline.', 'Clear boundaries help fans know what''s personal.', 'A stage pass isn''t an invitation into my home.', 'My phone stays off during family dinner.'),
('How important is loyalty in this industry?', 'Loyalty makes difficult years bearable.', 'I value people who keep promises when things go wrong.', 'Anyone who trades friends for a better headline loses my trust.', 'Ask me after our next contract negotiation.'),
('What do you do when music stops being fun?', 'I take a break and remember why I started.', 'We change the routine and try playing just for ourselves.', 'Sometimes you have to tear up the plan and jam.', 'I unplug everything and go for a walk.'),
('What matters more to you now than it did before the band became successful?', 'Time with people I care about means much more.', 'I pay closer attention to balance and stability.', 'Creative freedom matters more than collecting trophies.', 'An uninterrupted night''s sleep is pure luxury.'),
('What personal rule would you never break for success?', 'I wouldn''t betray a bandmate for a better deal.', 'We won''t promise fans something we can''t deliver.', 'I won''t let anyone buy the right to control our songs.', 'I refuse to mime a guitar solo.'),
('What''s something fame cannot give you?', 'Real friendship can''t be purchased with applause.', 'It can''t replace peace of mind or time at home.', 'Fame won''t make a weak song worth listening to.', 'It definitely can''t teach me to pack a suitcase.'),
('Do you prefer serious interviews or chaotic ones?', 'I like thoughtful questions that let us discuss the music.', 'A mixture of depth and humour works best.', 'A little chaos makes an interview memorable.', 'Ask me something bizarre and see what happens.'),
('Do you prepare answers before major interviews?', 'I think about the topics without scripting every word.', 'We agree on facts, then speak naturally.', 'Rehearsed answers sound worse than honest pauses.', 'Judging by this answer, clearly not enough.'),
('Do you trust music journalists?', 'I trust writers who listen carefully and quote fairly.', 'It depends on the publication and the individual.', 'I''ll trust a tough question more than a flattering agenda.', 'I trust them right up until the headline appears.'),
('Have you ever given an answer purely because you knew it would become a headline?', 'I''d rather answer truthfully than engineer a viral quote.', 'Sometimes I''m aware which phrases might travel far.', 'I''ve said provocative things knowing they''d make the front page.', 'Well, I was hoping you would ask that.'),
('Have you ever lied in an interview?', 'I''ve withheld details, but I try not to invent facts.', 'Sometimes protecting privacy means declining a question.', 'I once exaggerated a story to make it sound better.', 'No. Unless that answer counts.'),
('Is there a publication or show you still dream of appearing on?', 'I''d love a long-form programme that explores songwriting.', 'A major music magazine feature would be special.', 'Give us a live televised performance with no safety net.', 'Any show that lets me bring my own guitar.'),
('Should interviewers ask about an artist''s private life?', 'They can ask respectfully and accept a refusal.', 'It''s reasonable when private experiences shape the art.', 'Private lives shouldn''t become public property.', 'Ask about my pedals before my relationships.'),
('What''s the biggest thing the press gets wrong about your band?', 'They often mistake disagreement for internal conflict.', 'A headline can''t capture the work behind each song.', 'We''re not a manufactured image with instruments attached.', 'They keep saying the bassist is the quiet one.'),
('What''s the question you''re most tired of being asked?', 'People always ask when we''ll make our old sound again.', 'I hear the same questions about fame on every tour.', 'Stop asking whether rock is dead.', 'Apparently, this one is now a contender.'),
('Would you ever walk out of an interview?', 'Only if someone crossed a serious personal boundary.', 'I''d try to explain the problem before leaving.', 'If the questions turn cruel, I''ll end the conversation.', 'Ask about our snack budget again and find out.'),
('Do expensive studios really make better records?', 'Good songs and performances matter more than luxury rooms.', 'A great room helps, but creativity isn''t priced by the hour.', 'Some of the rawest records came from tiny studios.', 'An expensive sofa won''t fix a bad chorus.'),
('Do you listen to unfinished mixes outside the studio?', 'Yes, I test them on headphones and in the car.', 'Hearing a rough mix elsewhere reveals problems.', 'If it works on cheap speakers, we''re onto something.', 'I made everyone listen to the same chorus twenty times.'),
('Do you prefer recording quickly or obsessing over every detail?', 'I love capturing a great performance while it''s fresh.', 'We take enough time to fix what matters.', 'One extra take can make the difference between good and great.', 'Someone has to pry the headphones off me.'),
('Have you ever kept a technically imperfect take because it had more feeling?', 'Absolutely; the emotion can matter more than precision.', 'We compare takes and keep the one that connects.', 'A cracked note can tell more truth than a perfect one.', 'The mistake is probably my favourite part.'),
('How do you decide when to stop adding layers to a track?', 'When the arrangement already supports the song.', 'We mute parts and see what we actually miss.', 'If another overdub hides the hook, it has to go.', 'When the computer threatens to melt.'),
('How many versions of a song do you usually go through?', 'Sometimes the first demo survives nearly unchanged.', 'A few versions help us find the right shape.', 'We rewrite until the song surprises us.', 'I stopped counting after version seventeen.'),
('How much influence should a producer have over the band''s sound?', 'A producer should help us express our own ideas.', 'We welcome suggestions but keep final creative control.', 'A great producer challenges us without taking over.', 'Anyone asking to delete all the guitars gets a debate.'),
('Is recording more satisfying than performing live?', 'The studio lets us build details fans may discover later.', 'Recording and performing satisfy different parts of me.', 'Nothing beats a crowd singing a chorus back.', 'The studio has fewer flying drinks.'),
('What''s the biggest disagreement you''ve had during a recording session?', 'We once argued over whether a chorus needed another guitar.', 'The hardest debates usually involve the final mix.', 'Someone wanted to cut the part I thought made the song.', 'We spent two hours fighting over one cymbal hit.'),
('Would you ever record an entire album live in the room?', 'Yes, capturing everyone together could feel incredible.', 'We''d rehearse hard first and keep overdubs minimal.', 'A raw live album would show exactly what we can do.', 'Only if we''re allowed a second take when the drummer sneezes.'))
UPDATE public.interview_questions q SET option_a_text=t.a,option_b_text=t.b,option_c_text=t.c,option_d_text=t.d
FROM tailored t WHERE q.question_text=t.question_text AND q.created_at::date=DATE '2026-09-02';